tent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-15T14:25:20Z","updated_at":"2025-07-15T14:25:20Z","body":"@Calinou Just as a heads-up, I'm seeing some strange progress reports during `--headless --import` in the CI logs of a large project that I'm supporting, which seems to originate from this PR.\r\n\r\nIt seems the approach of caching the latest `p_steps` as `progress_total_steps` breaks down under certain circumstances (that I have yet to track down completely) which results in a bunch of greater-than-100% reports like this:\r\n\r\n```\r\n[1850% ] reimport | some_asset.png\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe flow of `EditorNode::progress_add_task` calls seems to be something along these lines:\r\n\r\n1. `first_scan_filesystem` with 5 steps.\r\n2. `update_scripts_classes` with 1822 steps.\r\n3. `_update_scan_actions` with 1880 steps.\r\n4. `reimport` with 1880 steps.\r\n    - The files aren't actually imported here, instead it prints \"Preparing files to reimport...\" for every file.\r\n5. `preload_reimporting_scene` with 1 step.\r\n6. Then the actual `reimport` tasks start processing, but with a borked percentage, due to `progress_total_steps` being `1`.\r\n\r\nI suspect that this `preload_reimporting_scene` probably shouldn't be happening in the first place, so I'll look into that, but I figured I should let you know anyway, since others might run into this as well.\r\n\r\nI'll make an issue with an MRP if/when I know more.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3073841730/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]